From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:57:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ext4: keep the allocator state of a group with inode
 preallocations in memory

Evicting a cached ext4 inode that still holds an inode preallocation
allocates memory from reclaim. ext4_clear_inode() calls
ext4_discard_preallocations(), which loads the group's buddy with
GFP_NOFS | __GFP_NOFAIL, and when the group's bitmap and buddy folios in
s_buddy_cache are no longer cached (drop_caches, or earlier reclaim),
__filemap_get_folio() has to allocate them. The inode shrinker runs
under PF_MEMALLOC, and since 903edea6c53f the page allocator warns about
a __GFP_NOFAIL request there whenever it misses the fast path:

  WARNING: mm/page_alloc.c:4763 __alloc_pages_slowpath
   __filemap_get_folio
   ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp
   ext4_discard_preallocations
   ext4_clear_inode
   ext4_evict_inode
   evict
   prune_icache_sb
   super_cache_scan
   shrink_slab
   balance_pgdat
   kswapd

The release also reads the group's block bitmap buffer, which is a
__GFP_NOFAIL allocation (__getblk_slow()) once the buffer is gone. The
flags cannot be dropped: a failure there would abort the filesystem.

Closed inodes hold preallocations more often than it seems. Enabling
fs-verity writes the Merkle tree past EOF without delayed allocation, so
the preallocation outlives the file's last close and only eviction
discards it.

Make the release not allocate. While a block group holds at least one
inode preallocation, it holds references to the group's in-core bitmap
folio, its buddy folio and its on-disk block bitmap buffer, kept in
struct ext4_group_info under the group lock together with a count of the
inode preallocations on bb_prealloc_list.

- The folios are taken when the count goes from 0 to 1 in
  ext4_mb_new_inode_pa(), where the allocation already holds both, so
  the references neither sleep nor fail.
- The buffer is taken by the first ext4_mb_mark_context() of the group
  while the count is non-zero, which is the call that marks the blocks
  of the same allocation. Until then the inode is in use by the
  allocating task and cannot be evicted.
- Every place an inode preallocation leaves bb_prealloc_list
  (ext4_mb_put_pa(), ext4_mb_discard_group_preallocations(),
  ext4_discard_preallocations() and ext4_mb_cleanup_pa() at unmount)
  decrements the count, and when it reaches zero detaches the references
  under the group lock and puts them after unlocking. ext4_mb_release()
  drops all of them before it puts the buddy cache inode.

The release then finds all three objects in memory:
ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp() takes its lock-free path and
ext4_read_block_bitmap() finds the buffer. A referenced folio is neither
dropped from the cache nor re-initialised by ext4_mb_init_cache(), which
skips an initialised group, so online resize and block sizes below the
page size (several groups share a folio) are unaffected. Locality group
preallocations are not counted, because eviction never releases them.

The cost is at most three 4 KiB pages per group that holds an inode
preallocation, 96 KiB per GiB of filesystem in the worst case, 32 bytes
per group in struct ext4_group_info, and the pinned pages cannot be
reclaimed or migrated while the preallocation lives. If the bitmap read
of the allocation fails, the group keeps no buffer reference and its
release falls back to reading the bitmap, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fs/ext4/ext4.h    |  12 ++++
 fs/ext4/mballoc.c | 140 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/ext4/ext4.h b/fs/ext4/ext4.h
index dae7fb8bc598e32311f4c64524709923805d94d1..1c1ccadc49a130baae9356448116e8869e1ea34c 100644
--- a/fs/ext4/ext4.h
+++ b/fs/ext4/ext4.h
@@ -3542,6 +3542,18 @@ struct ext4_group_info {
 	ext4_grpblk_t	bb_largest_free_order;/* order of largest frag in BG */
 	ext4_group_t	bb_group;	/* Group number */
 	struct          list_head bb_prealloc_list;
+	/*
+	 * While bb_prealloc_list holds inode preallocations, the group keeps
+	 * its allocator state in memory: references to its in-core bitmap and
+	 * buddy folios in s_buddy_cache and to its on-disk block bitmap
+	 * buffer, so that releasing an inode preallocation never allocates
+	 * (see ext4_mb_pa_refs_get() in mballoc.c).  All of this is protected
+	 * by the group lock.
+	 */
+	unsigned int	bb_inode_pa_count;	/* inode PAs on bb_prealloc_list */
+	struct folio	*bb_pa_bitmap_folio;
+	struct folio	*bb_pa_buddy_folio;
+	struct buffer_head *bb_pa_bitmap_bh;
 #ifdef DOUBLE_CHECK
 	void            *bb_bitmap;
 #endif
diff --git a/fs/ext4/mballoc.c b/fs/ext4/mballoc.c
index 71b8b47e213ab1775219fb49b142fa9d67556219..bef6cbb7ef74f5eabaaecd412e9efc05897f2262 100644
--- a/fs/ext4/mballoc.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/mballoc.c
@@ -3864,8 +3864,116 @@ int ext4_mb_init(struct super_block *sb)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-/* need to called with the ext4 group lock held */
-static int ext4_mb_cleanup_pa(struct ext4_group_info *grp)
+/*
+ * Releasing an inode preallocation must not allocate memory.  The inode
+ * shrinker releases one when it evicts a cached inode, and then it runs under
+ * PF_MEMALLOC, where the page allocator warns about the __GFP_NOFAIL request
+ * that ext4_discard_preallocations() makes for a buddy folio that is no
+ * longer cached, and a failing request would have to abort the filesystem.
+ *
+ * So while a group holds at least one inode preallocation, it also holds
+ * references to the three objects the release needs: the group's in-core
+ * bitmap folio and buddy folio in s_buddy_cache, and its on-disk block bitmap
+ * buffer.  The release then finds all of them in memory.  A referenced folio
+ * is neither dropped from the cache nor replaced by ext4_mb_init_cache(), and
+ * a referenced buffer is not freed.  The references are taken and dropped
+ * where an inode preallocation joins and leaves bb_prealloc_list, under the
+ * group lock for the pointers and outside it for the puts.
+ *
+ * The folios are taken from the allocation that creates the first
+ * preallocation, which already holds them.  The buffer is taken by the first
+ * ext4_mb_mark_context() of the group after that, which is the one that marks
+ * the blocks of the same allocation.  Until then the inode is in use by the
+ * allocating task, so it cannot be evicted.
+ *
+ * Locality group preallocations are not counted: nothing releases them from
+ * eviction.
+ */
+struct ext4_pa_refs {
+	struct folio *bitmap_folio;
+	struct folio *buddy_folio;
+	struct buffer_head *bitmap_bh;
+};
+
+/* Called with the group lock held when an inode PA joins bb_prealloc_list. */
+static void ext4_mb_pa_refs_get(struct ext4_group_info *grp,
+				struct ext4_allocation_context *ac)
+{
+	lockdep_assert_held(ext4_group_lock_ptr(ac->ac_sb,
+						ac->ac_b_ex.fe_group));
+	if (grp->bb_inode_pa_count++)
+		return;
+	WARN_ON_ONCE(grp->bb_pa_bitmap_folio || grp->bb_pa_buddy_folio ||
+		     grp->bb_pa_bitmap_bh);
+	/*
+	 * The allocation holds both folios until ext4_mb_release_context(), so
+	 * taking another reference neither sleeps nor fails.
+	 */
+	grp->bb_pa_bitmap_folio = ac->ac_bitmap_folio;
+	folio_get(grp->bb_pa_bitmap_folio);
+	grp->bb_pa_buddy_folio = ac->ac_buddy_folio;
+	folio_get(grp->bb_pa_buddy_folio);
+}
+
+/* Called with the group lock held, after the group's bitmap buffer is read. */
+static void ext4_mb_pa_refs_get_bitmap(struct ext4_group_info *grp,
+				       struct buffer_head *bitmap_bh)
+{
+	if (!grp->bb_inode_pa_count || grp->bb_pa_bitmap_bh)
+		return;
+	get_bh(bitmap_bh);
+	grp->bb_pa_bitmap_bh = bitmap_bh;
+}
+
+/* Move all of the group's references to @refs; the group lock is held. */
+static void ext4_mb_pa_refs_take(struct ext4_group_info *grp,
+				 struct ext4_pa_refs *refs)
+{
+	WARN_ON_ONCE(refs->bitmap_folio || refs->buddy_folio ||
+		     refs->bitmap_bh);
+	refs->bitmap_folio = grp->bb_pa_bitmap_folio;
+	refs->buddy_folio = grp->bb_pa_buddy_folio;
+	refs->bitmap_bh = grp->bb_pa_bitmap_bh;
+	grp->bb_pa_bitmap_folio = NULL;
+	grp->bb_pa_buddy_folio = NULL;
+	grp->bb_pa_bitmap_bh = NULL;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Called with the group lock held after @pa left bb_prealloc_list.  When the
+ * last inode PA left, the group's references move to @refs, which the caller
+ * puts with ext4_mb_pa_refs_put() after dropping the lock.
+ */
+static void ext4_mb_pa_refs_detach(struct ext4_group_info *grp,
+				   struct ext4_prealloc_space *pa,
+				   struct ext4_pa_refs *refs)
+{
+	if (pa->pa_type != MB_INODE_PA)
+		return;
+	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(!grp->bb_inode_pa_count))
+		return;
+	if (--grp->bb_inode_pa_count)
+		return;
+	ext4_mb_pa_refs_take(grp, refs);
+}
+
+static void ext4_mb_pa_refs_put(struct ext4_pa_refs *refs)
+{
+	if (refs->bitmap_folio)
+		folio_put(refs->bitmap_folio);
+	if (refs->buddy_folio)
+		folio_put(refs->buddy_folio);
+	if (refs->bitmap_bh)
+		brelse(refs->bitmap_bh);
+	memset(refs, 0, sizeof(*refs));
+}
+
+/*
+ * need to called with the ext4 group lock held; the group's references move
+ * to @refs, which the caller puts after dropping the lock.
+ */
+static int ext4_mb_cleanup_pa(struct ext4_group_info *grp,
+			      struct ext4_pa_refs *refs)
 {
 	struct ext4_prealloc_space *pa;
 	struct list_head *cur, *tmp;
@@ -3877,6 +3985,8 @@ static int ext4_mb_cleanup_pa(struct ext4_group_info *grp)
 		count++;
 		kmem_cache_free(ext4_pspace_cachep, pa);
 	}
+	grp->bb_inode_pa_count = 0;
+	ext4_mb_pa_refs_take(grp, refs);
 	return count;
 }
 
@@ -3888,6 +3998,7 @@ void ext4_mb_release(struct super_block *sb)
 	struct ext4_group_info *grinfo, ***group_info;
 	struct ext4_sb_info *sbi = EXT4_SB(sb);
 	struct kmem_cache *cachep = get_groupinfo_cache(sb->s_blocksize_bits);
+	struct ext4_pa_refs refs = {};
 	int count;
 
 	/*
@@ -3905,11 +4016,13 @@ void ext4_mb_release(struct super_block *sb)
 				continue;
 			mb_group_bb_bitmap_free(grinfo);
 			ext4_lock_group(sb, i);
-			count = ext4_mb_cleanup_pa(grinfo);
+			count = ext4_mb_cleanup_pa(grinfo, &refs);
 			if (count)
 				mb_debug(sb, "mballoc: %d PAs left\n",
 					 count);
 			ext4_unlock_group(sb, i);
+			/* before iput(s_buddy_cache) below */
+			ext4_mb_pa_refs_put(&refs);
 			kmem_cache_free(cachep, grinfo);
 		}
 		num_meta_group_infos = (ngroups +
@@ -4092,6 +4205,7 @@ ext4_mb_mark_context(handle_t *handle, struct super_block *sb, bool state,
 	struct buffer_head *gdp_bh;
 	int err;
 	unsigned int i, already, changed = len;
+	struct ext4_group_info *grp;
 
 	KUNIT_STATIC_STUB_REDIRECT(ext4_mb_mark_context,
 				   handle, sb, state, group, blkoff, len,
@@ -4124,7 +4238,11 @@ ext4_mb_mark_context(handle_t *handle, struct super_block *sb, bool state,
 			goto out_err;
 	}
 
+	grp = ext4_get_group_info(sb, group);
 	ext4_lock_group(sb, group);
+	/* Keep the buffer an inode preallocation's release will read. */
+	if (grp)
+		ext4_mb_pa_refs_get_bitmap(grp, bitmap_bh);
 	if (ext4_has_group_desc_csum(sb) &&
 	    (gdp->bg_flags & cpu_to_le16(EXT4_BG_BLOCK_UNINIT))) {
 		gdp->bg_flags &= cpu_to_le16(~EXT4_BG_BLOCK_UNINIT);
@@ -5166,6 +5284,8 @@ static void ext4_mb_put_pa(struct ext4_allocation_context *ac,
 	ext4_group_t grp;
 	ext4_fsblk_t grp_blk;
 	struct ext4_inode_info *ei = EXT4_I(ac->ac_inode);
+	struct ext4_group_info *gi;
+	struct ext4_pa_refs refs = {};
 
 	/* in this short window concurrent discard can set pa_deleted */
 	spin_lock(&pa->pa_lock);
@@ -5206,9 +5326,13 @@ static void ext4_mb_put_pa(struct ext4_allocation_context *ac,
 	 * we make "copy" and "mark all PAs" atomic and serialize "drop PA"
 	 * against that pair
 	 */
+	gi = ext4_get_group_info(sb, grp);
 	ext4_lock_group(sb, grp);
 	list_del(&pa->pa_group_list);
+	if (gi)
+		ext4_mb_pa_refs_detach(gi, pa, &refs);
 	ext4_unlock_group(sb, grp);
+	ext4_mb_pa_refs_put(&refs);
 
 	if (pa->pa_type == MB_INODE_PA) {
 		write_lock(pa->pa_node_lock.inode_lock);
@@ -5341,6 +5465,7 @@ ext4_mb_new_inode_pa(struct ext4_allocation_context *ac)
 	pa->pa_inode = ac->ac_inode;
 
 	list_add(&pa->pa_group_list, &grp->bb_prealloc_list);
+	ext4_mb_pa_refs_get(grp, ac);
 
 	write_lock(pa->pa_node_lock.inode_lock);
 	ext4_mb_pa_rb_insert(&ei->i_prealloc_node, &pa->pa_node.inode_node);
@@ -5509,6 +5634,7 @@ ext4_mb_discard_group_preallocations(struct super_block *sb,
 	LIST_HEAD(list);
 	struct ext4_buddy e4b;
 	struct ext4_inode_info *ei;
+	struct ext4_pa_refs refs = {};
 	int err;
 	int free = 0;
 
@@ -5561,6 +5687,7 @@ ext4_mb_discard_group_preallocations(struct super_block *sb,
 		spin_unlock(&pa->pa_lock);
 
 		list_del(&pa->pa_group_list);
+		ext4_mb_pa_refs_detach(grp, pa, &refs);
 		list_add(&pa->u.pa_tmp_list, &list);
 	}
 
@@ -5593,6 +5720,7 @@ ext4_mb_discard_group_preallocations(struct super_block *sb,
 	ext4_unlock_group(sb, group);
 	ext4_mb_unload_buddy(&e4b);
 	put_bh(bitmap_bh);
+	ext4_mb_pa_refs_put(&refs);
 out_dbg:
 	mb_debug(sb, "discarded (%d) blocks preallocated for group %u bb_free (%d)\n",
 		 free, group, grp->bb_free);
@@ -5617,6 +5745,8 @@ void ext4_discard_preallocations(struct inode *inode)
 	ext4_group_t group = 0;
 	LIST_HEAD(list);
 	struct ext4_buddy e4b;
+	struct ext4_group_info *grp;
+	struct ext4_pa_refs refs = {};
 	struct rb_node *iter;
 	int err;
 
@@ -5703,13 +5833,17 @@ void ext4_discard_preallocations(struct inode *inode)
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		grp = ext4_get_group_info(sb, group);
 		ext4_lock_group(sb, group);
 		list_del(&pa->pa_group_list);
+		if (grp)
+			ext4_mb_pa_refs_detach(grp, pa, &refs);
 		ext4_mb_release_inode_pa(&e4b, bitmap_bh, pa);
 		ext4_unlock_group(sb, group);
 
 		ext4_mb_unload_buddy(&e4b);
 		put_bh(bitmap_bh);
+		ext4_mb_pa_refs_put(&refs);
 
 		list_del(&pa->u.pa_tmp_list);
 		ext4_mb_pa_free(pa);
